        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Restringing a weed eater is a five-minute job once you know your head type. Wind in the direction of the arrow, keep the wraps tight and below the rim, load the length the manual specifies, and use the diameter the head was designed for.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Get those four things right and the problems people blame on their trimmer, line that welds, will not feed or snaps constantly, mostly go away. If your current head still fights you after that, a speed-load or auto-wind head is the single biggest quality-of-life upgrade you can make.
          </p>
